}\pard\plain\s0\qj\widctlpar\f0\fs20\sl240\slmult1 \sb300 \fi40 The activation energy of step R1 (glycerol dehydration to acrolein) has been reported in a wide range in literature. Talebian-Kiakalaieh et al. presented a value of 27.5 kJ/mol over tungstosilicic acid catalyst 
[{\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BIB_Talebian_Kiakalaieh2015 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{{39}{2015}{{Talebian-Kiakalaieh and Amin}}{{Talebian-Kiakalaieh, and Amin}}}}}
], Qadariyah et al. presented a value of 39.6 kJ/mol in sub-critical or supercritical water without any catalyst. 
[{\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BIB_Qadariyah2011 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{{45}{2011}{{Qadariyah et\~al.}}{{Qadariyah, Mahfud, Sumarno, Machmudah, Wahyudiono, Sasaki, and Goto}}}}}
] Watanabe et al. gave a value of 146 kJ/mol at 300-400 {{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ \\s\\up5({\fs16 {\u8728*}})}}{\fldrslt }}
}C with H{{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ \\s\\do5({\fs16 2})}}{\fldrslt }}
}SO{{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ \\s\\do5({\fs16 4})}}{\fldrslt }}
} catalyst 
[{\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BIB_Watanabe2007 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{{46}{2007}{{Watanabe et\~al.}}{{Watanabe, Iida, Aizawa, Aida, and Inomata}}}}}
], while Ott et al. report a value of 140 kJ/mol at 300-360 {{\field{\*\fldinst{ EQ \\s\\up5({\fs16 {\u8728*}})}}{\fldrslt }}
}C over zinc sulfate catalyst 
[{\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BIB_Ott2006 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{{47}{2006}{{Ott et\~al.}}{{Ott, Bicker, and Vogel}}}}}
]. Our result described in {\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BMT_Ea \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{Table\~ {}2}}} is in the reported range of 27.5-146 kJ/mol.\par
\pard\plain\s0\qj\widctlpar\f0\fs20\sl240\slmult1 \sb60 \fi40 The activation energy of step R2 is smaller than that of step R3 by 26 kJ/mol, indicating step R2 dominates in the reaction pathways, as compared to step R3. As a series reaction, step R4, with a slightly higher activation energy, is followed by step R2.\par
\pard\plain\s0\qj\widctlpar\f0\fs20\sl240\slmult1 \sb60 \fi40 All the present works were carried out under differential operating conditions, while integral conditions were applied in our prior work. 
[{\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BIB_Xiao2016 \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{{21}{2016}{{Xiao and Varma}}{{Xiao, and Varma}}}}}
] Now all kinetic parameters, including rate constants, reaction orders, activation energies and exponential factors, for steps R1-R4 are known. All the 80 data points for experimental and predicted flow rates are plotted in {\field{\*\fldinst{\lang1024 REF BMF_parity \\* MERGEFORMAT }}{\fldrslt{Figure\~ {}6}}}, giving an RMS error of 6.1%, indicating good fits.\par
